sequenceDiagram
    participant A as Client A
    participant B as Client B
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Note over A,DB: Both clients read the same task record simultaneously
    A->>DB: SELECT * FROM project_task WHERE id = 'task-1'
    DB-->>A: Returns { version: 1, status: 'TODO' }
    B->>DB: SELECT * FROM project_task WHERE id = 'task-1'
    DB-->>B: Returns { version: 1, status: 'TODO' }

    Note over A,DB: Client A updates first
    A->>DB: UPDATE project_task SET status='DONE', version=2\nWHERE id='task-1' AND version=1
    DB-->>A: Success (1 row affected) — version is now 2

    Note over B,DB: Client B attempts update with stale version
    B->>DB: UPDATE project_task SET title='New Title', version=2\nWHERE id='task-1' AND version=1
    DB-->>B: Failure (0 rows affected — version mismatch)

    Note over B: Client B detects race condition (OptimisticLockError)\nMust re-fetch latest version and retry
